<title>UK: NWE gasoline slips $1 after crude's tumble.</title>
<headline>NWE gasoline slips $1 after crude's tumble.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE gasoline was $1 weaker on Friday as screen crude's losses impacted. Dealers said mogas had resisted the drop on Thursday, but consolidation at the lower levels this morning meant gasoline had little option but to head lower.</p>
<p>Barges were down to $187 for eurograde fob ARA while cif cargoes were pegged at $192.00.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
